"Duncan Scott"] " had the fastest semi-final qualifier with 1:44.60, followed by American " [:a {:href "/athletes/147472"} "Kieran Smith"] ", Lithuanian " [:a {:href "/athletes/135056"} "Danas Rapsys"] ", and Scott’s teammates, " [:a {:href "/athletes/143201"} "Tom Dean"] ". Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144707"} "Katsuhiro Matsumoto"] " was the silver medallist in the 200 free at the 2018 Pan Pacs and the 2019 World Championships, and was a hometown favorite, but he finished in a tie for 16th in the heats, and although he won a swim-off, elected not to take part in the semi-finals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final Korea’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/145041"} "Hwang Seon-Wu"] " led through 100 metres, splitting 49.78, and maintained his lead through 150, but he had nothing left and would finish seventh. Behind him Dean and Brazil’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/141271"} "Fernando Scheffer"] " exchanged second and third to 150 metres, while Scott was only sixth at 100 metres, moving up to fourth at 150."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Scott closed the fastest 26.46 for the final 50 metres, as Scheffer faded, but Scott just missed catching Dean, who held on for the gold medal in 1:44.22, only 0.04 seconds ahead of Scott, as Britain went 1-2. Scheffer held on for the bronze, holding off Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/146364"} "David Popovici"] " by 2/100ths of second."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Scott, who had two relay medals from Rio, would add three more medals in Tokyo, with him and Tom Dean helping Great Britain win gold in the 4 x 200 free relay."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143201"} "Tom Dean"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.p